  "138": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the male lead character whose facial likeness, fair natural skin tone, dark short hair, and tailored charcoal jacket come from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> is the female lead character whose facial likeness, hairstyle, and ivory dress come from <Picture 2>.\n<Subject 3> is the warm theater stage environment shown in the keyframe anchors, preserving the exact lighting layout and camera perspective.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + keyframe completion] A continuous 4.0-second medium-full shot of <Subject 1> and <Subject 2> performing a synchronized duet interaction on <Subject 3>, following the motion rhythm of <Video 1> and transitioning smoothly through the anchored keyframes.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - exact facial identity and outfit from <Picture 1> are strictly retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - exact facial identity and outfit from <Picture 2> are strictly retained.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - stage geometry, lighting, and camera framing remain consistent without background switching.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a photorealistic 16:9 4K cinematic performance shot.\n[Shot 1] <Subject 1> on the left and <Subject 2> on the right step toward center stage. From 00:00.400 to 00:02.200, <Subject 1> sings expressively with clear lip sync while extending his right hand; <Subject 2> places her hand in his and turns smoothly into a side-by-side pose by 00:04.000. In <Picture 1> is the male lead; in <Picture 2> is the female lead. Clean background with only the two leads, zero text, zero watermarks.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nFrom 0.40s to 2.20s clear expressive male lead vocals matching mouth movements, followed by subtle stage footsteps and room ambience.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nWarm mid-tempo pop instrumental accompaniment.\n"
    },
    "class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Input Text (Prompt)"
    }
